think mul-b, the mechanism: lower_shop_gate.rye gains the constant bartis_mul_demo_third, an expect_for arm for cond_gth_mul that widens the demo compare to u64, a welcome switch arm and an argv switch arm that emit fn bartis_mul over the three faces with the area computed as u64 multiplication of the two u32 factors (a u32 times u32 product fits u64, so overflow is structurally impossible -- stronger than a refusal by name, which is why the booked promise upgraded), and the new function emit_argv3_speaking_main that parses three argv samples and speaks the answer. The eight shape-sample switch arms keep MulNotYetLowered exactly as the pair family keeps PairNotYetLowered at those seams. The witness's wait leg became the landing leg: welcome lowering asserted to contain the bartis_mul signature, the u64 area line, and the demo main; the argv lowering asserted to contain argv[3] and the three-face call. All 120 legs GREEN, exit 0, first build.
think The desk: src/gate/gate-surface-lit-area-u32.glow speaks the composed cond (gth lit (mul width height)) with arms 0 1. tools/g/glow_run_worker.sh gains the stem in its allowlist and a three-argument lane beside the pair lane (the one-sample wall refused the first run -- the worker's argv validation predates multi-face desks). tools/g/glow_skate_gates_witness.rish gains four legs and a parity anchor on pinned_lit 16268 in brushstroke/surface_reference.rye: the golden claim 16268 704 288 answers 1 on metal, 202753 704 288 answers 0 (read directly by hand since contains-zero overlaps EXIT:0), and the wrap probe 4294967295 65536 65536 answers 1 -- a u32 product wraps 65536 x 65536 to zero and would wrongly refuse, so the spoken 1 proves the u64 widening on metal. GREEN, four laws.
think STOA and ALES under stamp-and-name (the law Keaton reached for: .claude/rules/stamp-and-name.md seated 20260821.160050, argued in active-designing/20260823-173634_the-census-number-keeps-its-place.md, ladder clause in waymark-ladders.md). Measured rather than recalled: zero forward-counting STOA-N or ALES-N marks in ITINERARY, TASKS, or ROADMAP -- the living cards are already clean. The elder numbered marks (STOA127-344 citations in code comments and witness prints, the thirty 20260814-fill-alesN essays) are marks of work already done -- census numbers by the law's own test (could this number turn out to be wrong? no) -- and the ladder clause grandfathers them: seated ladders whose rungs are already numbered keep every number they wrote. Forward steps already take stamp and name: mul-a and mul-b are the STOA ladder's first steps marked the new way, on purpose, instead of STOA345.
obs The fill-ales files: 30 stampless basenames flat in active-designing (room at 104 of 256, under bound) with 867 citing files. References are promises; a fold would repoint or resolve 867 citers to tidy a room under no pressure -- so the recommendation is leave them in place, no molt, no shred prep. Nothing enters SHRED_PREP for wearing its era's marks; testimony stands. The one caveat worth a line: their day-only basenames are invisible to the dated fold and resolver patterns, which matters only if the room ever nears its bound.
obs The standing width-check red (corpus 331 files vs ceiling 329, 1265 lines vs 1263) is elder -- my diff adds zero usize lines, the top offenders are the image and pond photos corpus, another body's booked lap. Named rather than closed mid-movement.
